&lt;p&gt;DumpScope is a memory forensics desktop application built with Python, PyQt6, and Volatility3 — designed to streamline memory dump analysis with a wizard-driven UI instead of raw CLI commands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Features&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="features"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#features" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wizard UI walking through case setup to analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plugin ribbon for running Volatility3 plugins without memorizing syntax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;QThread-based workers keep the UI responsive during long-running analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQLite case storage — save and reopen investigations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automatic OS detection from the memory image&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process dumping directly from the UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
